<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/apple-pay/">Apple Pay</a> expanded <a href="https://www.apple.com/ph/wallet/">to the Philippines</a> today, which means iPhone and Apple Watch owners in the country can add supported debit and credit cards to the Wallet app for contactless payments.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2023/11/apple-pay-feature-dynamic-island.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-921515" /><br/>
Credit and debit cards can be added by opening the Wallet app and tapping on the "+" button. According to <a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/PHCreditCards/comments/1veg7mt/apple_pay_in_the_philippines_megapost/">users on Reddit</a>, supported banks include UnionBank, GoTyme, Metrobank, and Chinabank. Cards are verified using SMS or phone call.<br/>
<br/>
Once an eligible card is added to the Wallet app, it can be used at retail locations that support &zwnj;Apple Pay&zwnj;. Reddit users have been able to add their cards to Apple Wallet and make &zwnj;Apple Pay&zwnj; purchases at stores like Starbucks and 7-Eleven.<br/>
<br/>
